      },
      "findings": [
        {
          "source_quote": "τούτοις οὖν καὶ τοῖς διψυχήσασι διὰ τὰς πράξεις αὐτῶν μετάνοια ἔτι ἐστίν·",
          "english_quote": "Retain both invited groups, the response conditions, suffering without supplied willingness, and the explicit Spirit/Son statement.",
          "issue": "The unit's theological metadata claims to retain suffering and an explicit Spirit/Son statement, neither of which occurs anywhere in the selected S.8.ix source. This imports decisions from other units into this unit's source audit, although the reader text itself does not insert those assertions.",
          "suggested_revision": "Limit this unit's theological decision to the two groups offered repentance, the necessity of quick repentance, and the warning concerning persistent pleasure. Remove the suffering and Spirit/Son claims from this unit's metadata, or explicitly identify them as cross-unit information rather than features of this source. Any replacement metadata requires fresh review.",
          "severity": "minor"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "edition": "simplified",
      "verdict": "revise",
      "checks": {
        "complete_coverage": false,
        "no_added_claims": false,
        "names_and_negations": true,
        "speaker_attribution": true,
        "source_choices_and_notes": false,
        "terminology_policy": true
      },
      "findings": [
        {
          "source_quote": "Οἱ δὲ ἐπιδεδωκότες τὰς ῥάβδους τὰ μὲν δύο μέρη ξηρά, τὸ δὲ τρίτον χλωρόν",
          "english_quote": "The people whose rods were two-thirds dry and one-third green",
          "issue": "The simplified edition omits the act of handing in the rods, expressed by ἐπιδεδωκότες. Possession of rods with these proportions does not fully represent the source's identification of people by the rods they submitted.",
          "suggested_revision": "Consider: “The people who handed in rods that were two-thirds dry and one-third green”. Review the proposed wording afresh against the source before adopting it.",
          "severity": "minor"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "καὶ οὐκ ἐκολλήθησαν τοῖς δικαίοις",
          "english_quote": "stopped keeping company with the righteous.",
          "issue": "“Stopped” asserts that they previously kept company with the righteous. The selected clause states that they did not associate with the righteous; it does not explicitly assert cessation of an earlier association. Their earlier faithfulness does not itself establish that added history.",
          "suggested_revision": "Consider: “did not keep company with the righteous.” Review the replacement in its full sentence before adopting it.",
          "severity": "minor"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "τούτοις οὖν καὶ τοῖς διψυχήσασι διὰ τὰς πράξεις αὐτῶν μετάνοια ἔτι ἐστίν·",
          "english_quote": "Retain both invited groups, the response conditions, suffering without supplied willingness, and the explicit Spirit/Son statement.",
          "issue": "The theological metadata claims preservation of suffering and an explicit Spirit/Son statement absent from this selected unit. The simplification metadata compounds the same scope error by claiming preservation of “suffering without supplied willingness, the Spirit/Son identification and all twelve distinct mountain descriptions”; none of those features occurs in S.8.ix. These are inaccurate unit-level audit claims, not omissions that should be repaired by adding material to the translation.",
          "suggested_revision": "Remove the out-of-unit claims from both metadata blocks. Describe only distinctions actually present here, including rod submission and proportions, continued faith without its works, the two groups offered repentance, quick repentance, and the death warning. Alternatively, label broader statements explicitly as cross-unit information with their proper unit references. Revised metadata requires fresh review.",
          "severity": "minor"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The standard reader text covers the selected clauses faithfully; its revision need is inaccurate unit-level metadata. The simplified edition independently preserves the principal assertions, negations, repentance requirement, and warning, but omits rod submission and adds a prior association with the righteous. Both editions appropriately retain the selected conjunction and disclose its reported partial preservation and shorter alternative. The supplied reports support assessing that disclosure, not authenticating unseen manuscripts or certifying an exhaustive collation. No proposed replacement is automatically accepted."
}
